// `==` over two structs one of whose fields is a LIST OF STRUCTS. The list compares on
// its own (`L[] == L[]` RUNS since D751/D752) and a scalar-list field compares inside a
// struct (`{ kids: i32[] }` RUNS), but a struct-element list FIELD reaches
// `emitStructEqRec`'s field-code ladder with no arm and takes the ladder's floor,
// `emitProgram: unsupported struct field type in equality` (`wasmEmit.vl:11990`). The
// recursion in the motivating shape (`type T = { v: i32, kids: T[] }`, the tree every
// cycle-detection example is written over) is NOT an ingredient — a non-recursive `L[]`
// field refuses identically. Found 2026-09-01 by the identity proposal's cross-language
// critique (`docs/internals/identity-critique-crosslang.md` finding 8); filed as D1017.
// Should print true.
type L = { w: i32 }
type T = { v: i32, kids: L[] }
const a: T = { v: 1, kids: [{ w: 2 }] }
const b: T = { v: 1, kids: [{ w: 2 }] }
print(a == b)
